# Count EPC Scan Location (Hard Lock)

- The EPC scanning page is `CountInventoryScreen` at `mobile/carbon_wms/lib/ui/screens/count_inventory_screen.dart`.
- Navigation entry point is `InventoryHubScreen` at `mobile/carbon_wms/lib/ui/screens/inventory_hub_screen.dart`.
- The `COUNT` tile in `InventoryHubScreen` pushes `CountInventoryScreen`.

## Required agent behavior

- Any request about "Count EPC scanning" must target `CountInventoryScreen` first.
- Do not move or rename the Count EPC screen without explicit user approval.
- Keep the user navigation path stable: `Login -> Inventory Hub -> COUNT -> CountInventoryScreen`.
- If EPCs are not appearing, verify both:
  - Native RFID pipeline (Chainway/Zebra/native broadcasts)
  - Flutter ingestion on Count (`RfidManager`, vendor channels, Count listeners)

## Count-only trigger hard lock

- Scope: this behavior applies only on `CountInventoryScreen`.
- Handheld trigger must be toggle mode:
  - One press = start scanning.
  - Next press = stop scanning.
- Trigger must not require press-and-hold on Count.
- No scan session timeout or auto-stop timer is allowed on Count trigger flow.

## EPC duplicate policy hard lock (Count)

- Default Count behavior must treat each EPC as unique (one unit per EPC).
- Do not treat repeated reads of the same EPC as normal additional quantity.
- If the same EPC is observed multiple times, keep it visible and mark it as defective duplicate behavior.
- Repeated-sighting count should remain visible (for example, `xN`) to show how many times that same EPC repeated.
- Defective duplicate EPC repeats are not considered valid SKU/asset quantity growth.

## Audio feedback hard lock (Count default)

- Count scanning must provide audible feedback by default.
- Play a scan sound for each EPC scan event on Count.
- Play a distinct audible signal when scan mode starts and when scan mode stops from trigger/button toggle flow.
- Keep this behavior wired in-app so Count works reliably with device settings variations.

## Counter progression hard lock (Count)

- Count totals must progress one-by-one in visible sequence:
  - `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> ...`
- Do not allow visible jump-style counter progression such as:
  - `2 -> 5 -> 6 -> 8 -> ...`
- This rule applies to displayed Count totals during active EPC scanning.
- If needed, animate displayed totals in single-step increments so the user always sees sequential progression.

## RFID-only hard lock (Count)

- Count screen is RFID-only.
- 2D laser scanner must stay OFF at all times on Count.
- Never enable 2D scanning mode while on `CountInventoryScreen`.
- On entering Count and during active scan sessions, force-disable 2D scanner paths if the device tries to re-enable them.

## Count settings override hard lock

- On Count screen, the gear settings for `Antenna` and `RSSI` are authoritative.
- While inside Count, `Antenna`/`RSSI` values must override side-menu/global handheld settings.
- These Count-specific overrides must apply only to Count behavior.
- On leaving Count, revert control to side-menu/global settings automatically.
